------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Drawdown.  This is what WELDRAW limits, so these are the primary vectors.
-- WUDD is defined in the SCHEDULE section as WBP - WBHP and therefore gives
-- the drawdown directly; the limit is being honoured when WUDD sits on the
-- WELDRAW value while WMCTL reports the rate control mode the limit imposes.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WBHP
 /

WBP
 /

WUDD
 /

-- The alternative well block averaging procedures.  WBP is a plain average
-- while the limit itself uses a connection-transmissibility-weighted average,
-- so these differ slightly for wells completed in contrasting layers.
WBP4
 /

WBP5
 /

WBP9
 /

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Well control mode and status.  A well cut back by its drawdown limit
-- switches to the rate control the limit imposes: WMCTL 4 (LRAT) for a
-- liquid target phase, 3 (GRAT) for a gas target.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WMCTL
 /

WSTAT
 /

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rates.  The drawdown limit enters as a maximum rate for the target phase,
--
--     Qmax = Dmax * sum_j (Tw_j * M_j),
--
-- so while the limit is active the produced rate should reproduce as the
-- drawdown limit multiplied by the productivity index reported below:
-- WLPR / WPIL for a liquid target, WGPR / WPIG for a gas target.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WLPR
 /

WOPR
 /

WWPR
 /

WGPR
 /

WGOR
 /

WWCT
 /

WWIR
 /

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Productivity indices, i.e. the sum_j(Tw_j * M_j) factor of the conversion.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WPIL
 /

WPIG
 /

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Well potentials.  Item 4 of WELDRAW is NO in these cases, so the drawdown
-- limit must not enter the potential calculation: these should match the
-- base case even while the limit is cutting the rates back.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WOPP
 /

WGPP
 /

WTHP
 /

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Connection pressures, for inspecting the spread in drawdown across the
-- layers that the PI-weighted average of item 5 averages over.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CPR
 'D-1H' /
 'D-2H' /
/

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Pressure away from the wells.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RPR
 1 2 /

FPR

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Segment pressures and flows for the multisegment producer D-2H.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SPR
 'D-2H' /
/

SOFR
 'D-2H' /
/

SWFR
 'D-2H' /
/

SGFR
 'D-2H' /
/

